# Backend

FastAPI service for `{{projectName}}`.

## App structure

```
app/
├── core/           # settings, database session, shared utilities
├── fixtures/       # test fixture helpers
├── management/     # management / admin commands
├── models/         # SQLAlchemy ORM models
├── queries/        # database query functions
├── routers/        # APIRouter modules (one file per resource)
├── schemas/        # Pydantic request/response schemas
├── tasks/          # Celery task definitions
├── tests/          # pytest test suite
│   ├── models/
│   ├── queries/
│   ├── routers/
│   ├── tasks/
│   └── utils/
├── utils/          # pure helper functions
├── __init__.py
└── main.py         # entry point — routers, lifespan
```

Every source file in `models/`, `queries/`, `routers/`, `tasks/`, and `utils/`
must have a corresponding test file in `tests/<dir>/test_<name>.py`.
Run `dude lint` from the project root to check coverage.

## Requirements

- Python 3.13+
- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) (recommended)
- Docker (recommended for full-stack dev)
{{#if withPostgres}}
- PostgreSQL 17
{{/if}}
{{#if withCelery}}
- Redis 7
{{/if}}

## Run with Docker

```bash
docker compose up --build
```
{{#if withPostgres}}

Migrations run automatically on container start via `start.sh`.

To create a new migration after changing models:

```bash
dude db makemigration --message "describe change"
dude db migrate
```
{{/if}}
{{#if withCelery}}

Celery worker and{{#if withCeleryBeat}} beat scheduler and{{/if}} Flower monitor are started automatically by docker compose.
Flower UI: <http://localhost:5555>
{{/if}}

## Run locally (without Docker)

```bash
uv sync
uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
```

Then open <http://localhost:8000/api/health>.

